# 16. Research Priorities

The next phase should move beyond national statistics toward comparative case analysis.

Priority datasets should include:

### Stock-level dataset

Fields should include:

* stock name;
* species;
* region;
* management council;
* fishery management plan;
* stock status;
* overfishing status;
* overfished status;
* rebuilding status;
* rebuilding-plan date;
* rebuilt date;
* assessment frequency;
* biomass;
* fishing mortality;
* reference points;
* FSSI membership;
* FSSI score components;
* uncertainty;
* major habitat constraints.

### Rebuilding-case dataset

For selected rebuilt and rebuilding stocks:

* initial condition;
* cause of decline;
* management intervention;
* fishing reduction;
* habitat intervention;
* monitoring;
* biological response;
* rebuilding duration;
* institutional coordination;
* economic effects;
* residual threats;
* post-rebuilding management.

### Aquatic-system case studies

Particular attention should be given to:

* salmon and steelhead;
* Pacific bluefin tuna;
* Atlantic cod;
* Pacific sardine;
* Gulf of Mexico reef fishes;
* Atlantic highly migratory species;
* freshwater fish affected by dams;
* Tribal fisheries;
* interstate fisheries.

